      "description": "<p>Follow the day’s news live</p><p>One Nation has come up with a plan to give people their superannuation earlier, reducing the amount they’ll have at retirement in exchange for a current cash boost.</p><p><strong>Pauline Hanson</strong> says under their plan anyone paying rent or a mortgage can take up to a quarter of their super as a “pay boost” for up to three years.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/07/anthony-albanese-labor-lobbying-rules-greens-social-media-fines-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
