      "title": "Woman laid to rest in coffin made from mushrooms in Australian first",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/07/australian-woman-buried-in-mushroom-coffin-blue-mountains",
      "description": "<p>The casket, grown from mycelium and hemp fibres, takes just 45 days to break down, enriching the soil in the process</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/07/anthony-albanese-labor-lobbying-rules-greens-social-media-fines-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A woman has been buried in a coffin made from mushrooms in New South Wales in an eco-friendly first for Australia.</p><p>Carolyn, whose surname was withheld for privacy reasons, was laid to rest on Friday by friends and family at Springwood Cemetery in the Blue Mountains. She was aged in her 70s.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/07/australian-woman-buried-in-mushroom-coffin-blue-mountains\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-06T19:00:12"
    },
    {
      "title": "Greens criticise Labor after former IDF officer’s ‘reprehensible’ comments on Zomi Frankcom strike",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/07/zomi-frankcom-israel-gaza-idf-world-central-kitchen-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>David Shoebridge says ‘words are just distractions’ until government takes action</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/07/anthony-albanese-labor-lobbying-rules-greens-social-media-fines-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/05/aid-workers-gaza-killed-in-israel-airstrike-investigation\">‘Guilt by association’: why seven international aid workers were killed in Israeli airstrike</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The Greens have criticised inflammatory statements from the former Israel Defense Forces officer who ordered the attack that killed Zomi Frankcom, accusing the Albanese government of weakness over its failure to halt military exports and impose new sanctions.</p><p>Australian aid worker Frankcom and <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/21/australian-aid-worker-zomi-frankcom-idf-cleared-what-happened-ntwnfb\">six of her colleagues were killed in 2024</a> while bringing food to the people of <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/gaza\">Gaza</a>. Former IDF reserve colonel Nochi Mendel <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/05/aid-workers-gaza-killed-in-israel-airstrike-investigation\">has said</a> he would do “exactly the same thing” again and that those killed in the World Central Kitchen (WCK) humanitarian convoy in Gaza were “not innocent”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/07/zomi-frankcom-israel-gaza-idf-world-central-kitchen-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-06T15:00:10"
